# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- large, REGENERABLE artefacts -------------------------------------------------
# Excluded to keep the repo clonable, not because they do not matter. Each line says
# how to remake the thing, because "it is gitignored" and "it is lost" must not be the
# same sentence.

# 3D exports, 103 MB. Regenerate: JLC_LIB=<path> tools/export_3d.sh
# The STEP alone is 66 MB, over GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold.
cad/*.step
cad/*.glb
cad/tmp*.scad

# Historical board snapshots, 72 MB across 16 files. These are point-in-time copies
# taken before risky layout operations; git history now does that job properly.
.backup/

# SITL flight logs, 73 MB. Regenerate: bash sitl/run_scenarios.sh
sitl/logs/
sitl/terrain/*.DAT

# KiCad local state - per-user window layout and selection, not design data.
*.kicad_prl
_r.kicad_prl
_regress.kicad_prl
fp-info-cache

# KiCad backup written next to the board by an interrupted save.
*.kicad_pcb.bak

# Bench results are MEASUREMENTS of one physical board, not a property of the design.
# tools/check_rf.py deliberately fails until this exists; committing someone else's
# numbers would satisfy the gate without anyone having switched a board on.
fab/rf-bench-results.json
